CloudBurrow patch 38 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1457).

The bug: a CSV load stored every empty value as NULL, where BigQuery,
with a nullMarker set, "interprets the empty string as an empty value"
for STRING and BYTES columns (JobConfigurationLoad.nullMarker,
https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/rest/v2/Job#JobConfigurationLoad).
Its reader, encoding/csv, cannot tell "" from nothing, so CloudBurrow's
front, which reads a load's data by its options, could not load one.

The patch loads one value, U+FDD0 "cloudburrow:empty-string" U+FDD0, as
an empty string. The front writes an empty STRING or BYTES value under a
nullMarker as that value, and refuses a load whose data holds it.

